{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"edits\":[{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/1/text\",\"value_json\":\"Historical examples document use for a middle part or point in time or space. A separate proposal derives the “in the middle” sense from dividing an object; this does not establish a dated extension or show that the lexical sense “half” intervened.\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/1/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref014\\\",\\\"ref029\\\",\\\"ref030\\\",\\\"ref095\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/2/text\",\"value_json\":\"Historical examples document the “partial; incomplete” use. A separate proposal derives “incomplete” from dividing an object; its date and relation to the lexical sense “half” are unresolved.\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/senses/2/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref014\\\",\\\"ref029\\\",\\\"ref030\\\",\\\"ref095\\\"]\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/limitations/0/text\",\"value_json\":\"The proposed starting points conflict: “split/open” may have developed into “half,” or “half” may have been original. A separate proposal derives the “middle” and “incomplete” senses from dividing an object, but does not establish a dated sequence or show that the lexical sense “half” intervened. Historical examples document midpoint, partial or incomplete, and “very little,” but do not establish chronological links among these meanings.\"},{\"path\":\"meaning_history/limitations/0/evidence_ids\",\"value_json\":\"[\\\"ref014\\\",\\\"ref022\\\",\\\"ref029\\\",\\\"ref030\\\",\\\"ref095\\\",\\\"ref096\\\"]\"}]}"}}
